    SPDataFieldTypeSchema = external_exports.enum(["TEXT", "TEXTAREA", "NUMBER", "BOOLEAN", "DATE", "DATETIME", "TIME", "DATE_RANGE", "NUMBER_RANGE", "SELECT", "SELECT_MULTI", "AUTOCOMPLETE", "AUTOCOMPLETE_MULTI", "ATTACHMENT", "ATTACHMENT_MULTI"]).describe("Generic dynamic-field contract \u2014 a data-driven descriptor of ONE form/filter field, shared by FE and BE. A field is fully described by its `SPDataFieldConfig` (a polymorphic, `mtype`-discriminated object that carries the label/description/info/required metadata AND the type-specific options + validation constraints). The FE (`DSDataFieldForm`) renders the matching DS control straight from the config; the BE turns the same config into its validator. Values are the parallel `SPDataFieldValue` variants. One field type per control/value shape: every `mtype` maps 1:1 to a config + value variant, and each variant redeclares `mtype` as its own literal so the object is a true discriminated shape. Fields that share a value shape but differ only in input FORMAT (plain/url/email/phone text) are ONE `mtype` (TEXT) with a `textType` format subtype rather than separate types.");
    SPDataFieldTextTypeSchema = external_exports.enum(["PLAIN", "URL", "EMAIL", "PHONE"]).describe("Input-format subtype for a TEXT field \u2014 drives the input mode/type and format validation in the FE (e.g. EMAIL \u2192 email keyboard + email validator, PHONE \u2192 tel, URL \u2192 url). PLAIN is an unconstrained string.");
