    SPAuthPassportSchema = external_exports.object({}).describe('Marker interface for a serialized auth context \u2014 the queue-safe projection of an SPAuthUser carried on SPAuthenticatedEvent. A consumer rehydrates the actor from it (via `ISPAuthProvider.prepareAuthUser`) and runs service methods under `withAppExecutionContext`, i.e. "on behalf of" the principal who emitted the message. Implementations carry only the stable identity/scope ids needed to reconstruct the user \u2014 never secrets, sessions, devices, or anything volatile about the actor, such as what they may do or what their organization is offered. All of that is resolved again at rehydrate, because a queued message can sit for a long time and a snapshot would let the work run under an answer that has since changed. All context types must extend this interface.');
